00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:02.550 align:start position:0%
 
picking someone to take over a role from  another actor  is never easy especially when the  original performer drew praise for their  take on that character  but recasting is often unavoidable  especially for sequels and remakes  here are some more role replacements  that ruined movies  roger moore and sean connery each made  seven appearances as james bond though  many double 07 fans will tell you that  connery is the only bond  a cbs news poll concluded that 51  of americans chose connery as their  favorite bond with pierce brosnan  coming in a distant second george lesnbe  the man who replaced connery in the role  for 1969's on her majesty's secret  service received just one percent of the  vote which tells you  everything you need to know about the  gulf between these two actors  while critical opinion toward the film  itself has softened over time  lazenby's performance is still a bone of  contention  inevitably compared to those delivered  by connery in the franchise's five  previous entries the chicago reader said  that george lesinbee  has so much reserve as james bond that  he makes sean connery seem almost  frenetic by comparison reviews in the uk  were just as critical of the leading  man's turn as the british  secret service agent with london-based  outlet time  out calling him a stunning non-entity  fronting a film  with no redeeming features following in  the footsteps of linda hamilton  as sarah connor in the terminator  franchise was never going to be easy  she gave a performance so layered and  compelling that even the most  talented of actresses would have  struggled to do the character justice  a volunteer why  there's a chance to meet the legend  sarah connor the first to give it a shot  was lena heady who was cast as the  titular heroine  in the short-lived tv series terminator  the sarah connor chronicles  fox canceled the show after two seasons  leaving hidy's game of thrones colleague  emilia clark to carry the torch  2015's terminator genesis was heavily  criticized for using that old  time travel chestnut to rewrite the  beginning of the terminator story to  suit the filmmaker's purposes  the main problem however wasn't the  infuriatingly muddled timeline it was  the casting  veteran film critic peter bradshaw  dressed down the whole main cast in his  one star review for the guardian calling  amelia clark's take on connor  uninteresting 1981's the clash of the  titans attempted to give greek mythology  the star wars treatment  taking the story of perseus and turning  it into a sprawling epic  director desmond davis went with harry  hamlin in the role of perseus a son of  zeus who in legend beheads the gorgon  medusa in order to save his beloved  princess andromeda from a giant kraken  hamlin remains active in the industry  though he's still arguably best  remembered for his turn as perseus  the same cannot be said for sam  worthington best known as the star of  james cameron's budding avatar franchise  director louis leteriae entrusted the  australian with the lead role in his  2010 remake though his choice was called  into question when the negative reviews  started to pour in  worthington's earned his share of a  claim over the years but the titans  remake is one release he most likely  wouldn't mind leaving off his resume  quickflix's simon morado  questioned how worthington had ever  managed to become a hollywood actor  after watching his performance as  perseus in which  he does nothing but glare his battle  speeches are neither rousing nor  particularly intelligible despite its  name 1984's friday the 13th part for the  final chapter was far from the last  installment in this long-running horror  franchise in fact eight more films have  been made since the so-called final  chapter though the one that directly  followed it marked a major drop-off in  quality  part 4 has been described as one of the  last really excellent horror romps that  focus  on character dynamic and family felix  vasquez of cinema crazed  praised corey feldman for his standout  performance as young tommy jarvis  feldman went on to make a name for  himself in the goonies stand by me and  the lost boys though before he did he  reprised his friday the 13th role in  1985's part 5 a new beginning  unfortunately he only appeared in the  prologue and a time jump meant he was  replaced by the painfully dull john  shepard  teenage tommy was static compared to his  younger self though  shepard shouldn't shoulder the blame  entirely some blamed what they called  the ham-fisted directing of david  steinman while james kendrick of q  network argued that  the gory antics are so restrained by the  insistence of the mpaa rating system  that the film  feels like it was edited with one of  jason's bloody rusty weapons  wesley snipes rejected the opportunity  to return as willie mays hayes in 1994's  major league two  because he had become a movie star in  his own right by then with the cleveland  indians down a man  the filmmakers turned to omar epps  director david  s ward had worked with epps on the  program the previous year  which was a sports movie following the  exploits of a college football team  the big difference between the two films  however was that the program wasn't  meant to be funny  epps didn't have a background in comedy  and it showed in his timing  even those who didn't think the film was  all that bad admitted that  omar epps taking over for wesley snipes  was a complete  bomb of a decision bad all around  veteran film critic mark kermode summed  up 2015's the transporter refueled with  a single question  what exactly is the point of a  transporter movie without jason statham  when it was revealed that ed sprin was  to replace statham as special forces op  turned private driver frank martin in  the fourth transporter film  questions were raised about the former's  ability to carry the franchise forward  though the transporter films didn't  exactly change the action movie  landscape they benefited from statham's  presence athletic prowess and combat  skills  his replacement lacked that experience  and it showed skren began taking classes  in various martial arts disciplines as  he prepared for both the transporter  refueled and his role as ajax in  deadpool but  even he acknowledged that he was way  behind many of his peers in that  department  he told the bbc i'm very respectful and  realize i'm not going to be able to do  things meant for 10 or 20 years of  training  the action in the transporter refueled  was ultimately limited by the nustar's  fledgling abilities  ed skrinn's one and only outing as frank  martin was a commercial and critical  flop  that left the luke basson produced  franchise dead in the water  rooney mara took the role of androgynous  computer hacker liz beth salander  starring opposite daniel craig in 2011's  the girl with the dragon tattoo when the  2018 sequel the girl in the spider's web  was announced  fans of david fincher's critically  acclaimed first film were a little  disappointed that both mara and craig  had been recast  and so was mera she told yahoo i was  hopeful to come back  but they decided to do a different thing  it was always a character i wanted to  revisit but that's not what happened  severe goodness and replaced daniel  craig while claire foy stepped into the  pale  pierced skin of cylander unfortunately  she didn't look comfortable in it at the  time she was receiving a claim for her  turn as the young queen elizabeth ii  in the crown but foy couldn't pull off  salander's cold eccentricities with the  same poise as her predecessor  critics were by and large unimpressed  with her version of the goth hacker with  many questioning why she was chosen for  the part  the observers wendy eyde said much as i  admire her  foy is miscast here she's just too  empathetic for a role that requires an  almost reptilian lack of emotion  indie wires senior film critic david  ehrlich called her both  terrible and terribly miscast the first  robocop stars peter weller as the  titular cyborg  he roams a dystopian crime ridden  version of detroit mercilessly dealing  with lawbreakers  weller reprised the role in robocop 2  but turned down the chance to play him  again in a third movie  producers needed a replacement and their  hearts were apparently set on a  little-known actor named robert john  burke  in a 2015 interview burke said in god's  great earth they thought i was the only  actor who could do it  i don't know why i think physically i  poked like peter weller and i had also  had  extensive karate training pantomime  training and body training and i fit the  suit  unsurprisingly handing the lead role  over to the relatively inexperienced  perk just because he kind of resembled  weller didn't work out very well  he may have looked like him in the suit  but as the new york times said in its  review of the box office  bomb burke is lacking his forerunners  tongue-in-cheek glint of authoritarian  machismo  you have the right to an attorney what  is it  from his delivery to the way he moved  burke just wasn't as convincing as  robocop  as empire noted he appeared to be a lot  less comfortable with the hardware  1988's big is often cited as tom hanks  breakout movie but he actually announced  himself as a potential star some four  years earlier in ron howard's fantasy  rom-com  splash hanks plays alan bauer a young  man who returns to the spot of what he  believes was a near-death hallucination  to discover that the woman he saw in the  water the day he almost drowned is  indeed real  allen falls for mermaid madison and  ditches his life on land to live  under the sea with her in a goofy yet  undeniably feel-good ending  it's a beloved movie though the same  cannot be said about the obscure made  for tv sequel  splash 2. helmed by writer director and  actor greg  antonacci the highly forgettable and  completely unnecessary splash 2 brought  allen and madison back to dry land  totally ignoring the fact that the  government wanted to lock her up in a  lab in the previous installment  todd waring took over as alan bauer but  despite his best efforts  he lacked the every man charm and  comedic timing that was abundant in  hank's  filmfad said in its review of the sequel  the less said about the actors replacing  tom hanks and john candy the better  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one

